• **#978 (--save-session), commented and closed.** Commit `2c5ad8b2` adds the flag for both `-p` and piped runs. It writes the same JSON `/save` writes, and it also saves after a failed turn. It never creates a missing directory. An unwritable path exits non-zero, and if the turn had already failed, its own exit code is kept. In the comment I also noted one limit: a run killed from outside (for example by timeout) never gets to save.
